 days, which adds about 290 in holding for nothing in return.\n- Among the 3-day plans, candidates 4 and 5 carry even more stock than candidate 0, and candidate 6 has a smaller buffer. All of them lose to candidate 1 by about 300–400.\n\n**Randomness: candidate 1 against candidate 2.** These two are close.\n- Candidate 1 orders about 1.08 times forecast demand. Its stock arrives earlier within each 2-day cycle, so for the same amount ordered it runs short less often than daily ordering does.\n- Candidate 2 orders about 1.10 times forecast. That gives a slightly bigger buffer, but the extra stock costs about 190 more in holding for product 1. Each additional unit is worth roughly zero on average, because it only pays off when demand comes in high.\n- Both plans line up arrivals with expected demand right up to day 29. Neither risks writing off stock or exceeding the 200-unit warehouse limit.\n\nOverall, candidate 1 comes out ahead of candidate 2 by roughly 70–250, and ahead of the rest by a wider margin."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 358, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5754, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 358}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-26T08:58:24.057Z", "request_id": "req_011CgQa3Xj2zWyKbqnUPzbWX"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01UTfWYByoU3thxGbUSbgrHd", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-